=20
without external quantifiers as representing collective use, since those wi=
th=20
quantifiers are always distributive, but, convenient as that would be (to a=
void=20
questions about who carried the piano, say), there is greater convenience (=
it is=20
said) in the present system, which allows for the double use and also for c=
ases=20
where we just don't know where we don't know (or it doesn't matter) how the=
=20
group pulled it off.
But that, of course, is separate from the issue about {-mei}.  L-sets are a=
=20
